4. What are the different data types in python? With example.
A: 1) Number - int, float, complex
2) Text - string
A string starts and ends with double quotes " ".
3) Sequences
a) Lists - A list is a heterogeneous collection of elements. It starts and ends with square brackets [].
b) Tuples - It starts and ends with parentheses ()
4) Sets
A set is an unordered collection of elements. It has no duplicate element in it. It starts and ends with curly
brackets {}. It is a mutable data type.
5) Dictionary
A dictionary is denoted by dict. It is a combination of key and value pairs. It provides a mapping of keys to values.
6) Boolean type
It has two values - true and false.
7) Null data type - it means the variable is empty.


